{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>If the anointed priest.</b> Since he is a high priest, he brings a bull, which is the largest of all the offerings on the altar." "<b>To the guilt of the people.</b> To hold the people guilty, for he instructed and permitted them something forbidden; and we find that it is incumbent upon them to instruct, as it is written: יורו משפטיך ליעקב etc." "<b>For his sin.</b> On account of his sin, and as an example to atone for him — כי עליך הורגנו כל היום (for Your sake we are killed all the day)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:53.600839663Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}